{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Moses went in, and Aaron, etc.</b> Why did they enter? I found in the parashat millu'im, in the baraita appended to our Torat Kohanim: Why did Moses enter with Aaron? To teach him the procedure of the incense offering — or did he enter only for something else? I shall reason: descent and entry require a blessing; just as descent is in the category of avodah, so entry is in the category of avodah — from this you have learned why Moses entered with Aaron: to teach him the procedure of the incense offering. Another interpretation: Since Aaron saw that all the offerings had been brought and all the procedures done, yet the Shekhinah did not descend to Israel, he was distressed and said: I know that the Holy One, blessed be He, is angry with me, and on my account the Shekhinah has not descended to Israel. He said to Moses: Moses my brother, is this what you did to me — that I entered and was put to shame? Immediately Moses entered with him and they sought mercy, and the Shekhinah descended to Israel (Sifra)." "<b>And they went out and blessed the people.</b> They said: ״וִיהִי נֹעַם ה' אֱלֹהֵינוּ עָלֵינוּ״ — May it be Your will that the Shekhinah rest upon the work of your hands. For all seven days of the millu'im, during which Moses set up the Mishkan and served in it and disassembled it each day, the Shekhinah did not rest in it, and Israel were humiliated and said to Moses: Moses our teacher, all the effort we exerted so that the Shekhinah would rest among us and we would know that the sin of the calf was atoned for us — therefore he said to them: ״זֶה הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה' תַּעֲשׂוּ וְיֵרָא אֲלֵיכֶם כְּבוֹד ה'״ — Aaron my brother is worthy and more distinguished than I, for through his offerings and his avodah the Shekhinah will rest upon you, and you will know that the Omnipresent has chosen him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:40.815746905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}